  "slug": "mitochondrial-resource-16ed",
  "summary": "Recent preprints address selection bias in GWAS, replicability from summary statistics, and survival-based resilience genes in irradiated macaques.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the validity of association inference when standard analyses may be distorted. A review of ten methods addresses selection bias in GWAS, organized by selection type and data availability. KDRD estimates replicability of significant associations from one study's summary statistics, tested on UK Biobank. Restricted-mean survival pseudo-observations are applied to exome variants in irradiated rhesus macaques to identify resilience-associated genes linked to fibrosis and longevity. Other entries extend this concern in different directions: uniformly re-analysed public exercise omics contrasts are pooled through random-effects meta-analysis, and NMR-derived metabolic trajectories are examined against incident acute myocardial infarction in the UK Biobank. What is new is the emphasis on correcting or quantifying bias and testing reproducibility before interpreting associations.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-10"
}
